'''''Oceaniopteris gibba''''', the '''miniature tree fern''' ([[Synonym (taxonomy)|syn.]] '''''Blechnum gibbum'''''),<ref name=CFLW/> is a tropical species of fern in the family [[Blechnaceae]], [[native species|native]] to [[New Caledonia]] and introduced in [[Fiji]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Blechnum gibbum (Labill.) Mett. {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:17059040-1 |access-date=2022-05-25 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref>  It has received the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref name = RHSPF>{{cite web | url = https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/2311/Blechnum-gibbum/Details | title = ''Blechnum gibbum'' | website = www.rhs.org | publisher = Royal Horticultural Society | accessdate = 12 April 2020}}</ref> 

It grows to {{convert|1-2|m|ft|abbr=on}}. With a vertical "trunk" (actually a [[rhizome]]), it has bright green fronds. As it does not tolerate temperatures below {{convert|15 |C|F|abbr=on}}, in [[temperate climate|temperate]] zones it must be cultivated under glass all year round. It is a suitable subject for a greenhouse or conservatory. It requires an [[acid soil]] and a partially shaded position.<ref name = RHSPF/> 

